## How to read this

- **Risk-pts** = `BLAST_RADIUS × LIKELIHOOD × DISCOVERABILITY` per [RISK-SCORING.md](../references/methodology/RISK-SCORING.md). Range: 1-125 per site.
- **Trend arrows** = ▼ decreasing (good direction); ▶ stable; ▲ increasing (drift accruing).
- **(A) sites are obligations** — they stay; the audit hardens their SAFETY comments + adds clippy lints.
- **(B) sites are gated** by the `safe-only` Cargo feature; downstream users can opt in to the safe path at the documented perf cost.
- **(C) sites are refactor work-in-progress** — eliminate the unsafe via safe-Rust equivalent + property-test equivalence proof.
- **`pre-existing-ub-N`** = UB found during audit but OUTSIDE the current refactor scope; tracked separately to avoid scope creep.

For methodology details: [SKILL.md](../../SKILL.md). For the most recent audit's summary: [audit/AUDIT_SUMMARY.md](../audit/AUDIT_SUMMARY.md).

